<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//DITA Bootstrap//DTD DITA Bootstrap Topic//EN" "bootstrap-topic.dtd">
<topic id="buttons">
  <title>Buttons</title>
  <shortdesc>Use Bootstrap’s custom button styles for actions in forms, dialogs, and more with support for multiple
    sizes, states, and more.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Buttons</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>xref</xmlelement></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section id="base-class">
      <title>Base class</title>
      <p>Buttons have a standard <codeph>btn</codeph> class that sets up basic styles such as padding and content
        alignment, along with fallback visual styles for basic accessibility. Change this class to another button
        class to apply different visual styles for a specific button variant and theme.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Base class</title>
      <image href="src/buttons/base-class.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/buttons/base-class.xml"/></codeblock>

    <section id="example">
      <title>Example</title>
      <p>Bootstrap includes several predefined button styles, each serving its own semantic purpose, with a few extras
        thrown in for more control.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Example</title>
      <image href="src/buttons/example.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/buttons/example.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/buttons/example.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section id="variants">
      <title>Variants</title>
      <p>Compare the solid (default), outline, subtle, and text button styles at once, combined with theme
        colors.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Variants</title>
      <image href="src/buttons/variants.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/buttons/variants.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/buttons/variants.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section id="styled-buttons">
      <title>Styled buttons</title>
      <p>Add visual depth to solid buttons with gradients and shadows using the <codeph>btn-styled</codeph> modifier
        class. This provides a more three-dimensional appearance that can be customized further with CSS
        variables.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Styled buttons</title>
      <image href="src/buttons/styled-buttons.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/buttons/styled-buttons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/buttons/styled-buttons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section id="outline-buttons">
      <title>Outline buttons</title>
      <p>In need of a button, but not the hefty background colors they bring? Replace the default modifier classes with
        the <xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt> and a value of <codeph>btn-outline-*</codeph> to remove all background images
        and colors on any button.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Outline buttons</title>
      <image href="src/buttons/outline-buttons.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/buttons/outline-buttons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/buttons/outline-buttons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="sizing">
      <title>Sizing</title>
      <p>Fancy larger or smaller buttons? Use <xmlatt>size="large"</xmlatt>, <xmlatt>size="small"</xmlatt>, or
          <xmlatt>size="xs"</xmlatt> for additional sizes.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Sizing</title>
      <image href="src/buttons/sizing.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/buttons/sizing.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/buttons/sizing.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

<fig>
